c({id:"ApplicationController:5",text:"Navigation\nThree navigation methods serve different purposes:\n\njavascript\n// Push a menu by id \u2014 silent (does not update the URL hash)\nthis.pushMenu('admin.users');\nthis.pushMenu('admin.users', true);  // force reload even if already current\n\n// Update the URL hash \u2014 triggers routeUpdated listener, which calls pushMenu_\nthis.routeTo('admin.users');\nthis.routeTo('admin.users/42');      // menu + record id\n\n// Navigate to whichever menu owns a given DAO (and optionally a record)\nthis.routeToDAO(this.userDAO, userId);\n\n\nroute is declared memorable: true, so the URL hash is the source of truth. On page load, onUserAgentAndGroupLoaded reads this.route and calls either pushDefaultMenu() or routeUpdated() to restore the last location.\n\npushMenu does not update the URL; routeTo does. The distinction matters when you need deep-link support (use routeTo) vs. internal navigation that shouldn't affect the browser history (use pushMenu).",sourceId:"ApplicationController",kind:"flow",embeddingModel:"Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",vector:[-0.05559543,-0.07616824,0.0049869437,-0.021236656,-0.06800417,-0.06939915,-0.029903416,0.0046540354,-0.029796258,-0.005377446,-0.0102227675,0.080795735,-0.030594958,-0.039218094,0.0058471565,0.03640736,0.0137604885,0.049962677,-0.045712426,-0.022354277,0.10440548,-0.04563495,0.020649895,0.019039541,-0.04531879,-0.059539374,0.0475872,-0.039953284,0.0041659013,0.008997659,0.04101614,0.007070577,-0.1196492,-0.13314798,-0.10574306,0.0072658244,-0.020837545,-0.0337966,-0.039403826,-0.030321,-0.0015738537,0.0848159,-0.013394967,0.045289487,-0.012265333,-0.016842153,-0.046742283,0.10205779,-0.010211769,0.03732033,0.05527551,-0.005750555,-0.01624665,0.014447922,0.01683983,0.066333726,-0.077308975,0.03522296,-0.037014514,9.6371665E-4,-0.030552557,-0.02999445,0.0393467,-0.018119056,0.040579937,-0.056032013,0.026375517,-0.098724216,-0.03611679,0.014326169,0.05901408,-0.02959926,0.055626445,0.046233