c({id:"Axioms:6",text:"Notes\nAxioms are stored in axiomMap on each class, with inheritance handled through prototype chaining of the axiom maps. 6  When axioms are installed on parent classes, child classes are notified via pub/sub to clear their axiom caches. 18  The Relationship axiom is a specialized example that defines relationships between models. 19\n\nWiki pages you might want to explore:\n- Advanced Features and Extensions (foam-foundation/foam3)\n\nCitations\n\nFile: src/foam/lang/Boot.js (L54-56)\njavascript\n  Models are defined as a collection of Axioms.\n  It is the responsibility of Axioms to install itself onto a Model's Class and/or Prototype.\n\nFile: src/foam/lang/Boot.js (L58-64)\njavascript\n  Axioms are defined with the following psedo-interface:\n<pre>\n    public interface Axiom {\n      optional installInClass(cls)\n      optional installInProto(proto)\n    }\n</pre>\n\nFile: src/foam/lang/Boot.js (L85-97)\njavascript\n  However, raw axioms are rarely used directly. Instead we model higher-level\n  axiom types, including:\n<ul>\n  <li>Requires   - Require other classes\n  <li>Imports    - Context imports\n  <li>Exports    - Context exports\n  <li>Implements - Declare interfaces implemented / mix-ins mixed-in\n  <li>Constants  - Add constants to the prototype and class\n  <li>Properties - High-level instance variable definitions\n  <li>Methods    - Prototype methods\n  <li>Topics     - Publish/sub topics\n  <li>Listeners  - Like methods, but with extra features for use as callbacks\n</ul>",sourceId:"Axioms",kind:"flow",embeddingModel:"Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",vector:[-0.059133388,-0.07379787,0.030395659,-0.036117792,0.09470228,0.01353022,-0.057164636,0.06043382,-0.029955711,-0.044155683,0.027383082,0.01559548,0.009162223,0.005920902,0.06284319,0.03407404,0.057249434,-0.022254039,-0.04863057,0.0011710166,0.07640662,-0.023313638,-0.0044047753,-0.01886462,-0.04555901,0.044437256,0.05424448,-0.049513254,-0.049803406,-0.009322641,-0.01553712,0.05