c({id:"Context:1",text:"What is a Context?\nA context looks very much like a map, and behaves like a map, except it has inhertitance.\n\nMethods on context - \n\n1. x.get(\u2018key\u2019)\n\tIf there is a value associated with that key, it is returned, else null.\n2. x.put(key,value)\n\tThis returns a new context x\u2019, with all the values of the old context plus the new key pair\n\tcontext is immutable, putting will always return a new (sub)context.\n\tThis is important, because we do lots of gets, and so we don\u2019t have to lock it because it\u2019s immutable.\n3. x.putFactory(key, factory)\n\tWhen you call a get on this key, it will return the return value of the factory.\n\tOne additional feature here is, the factory gets the context you call it from, and runs with that context - so it can be aware of who is calling it.",sourceId:"Context",kind:"flow",embeddingModel:"Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",vector:[-0.067571506,0.012529416,-0.02363908,-0.029226823,0.0028044283,-0.013960172,0.10502393,0.01745005,-0.039081052,-0.045676403,0.08600769,-0.023146458,0.05193818,-0.06972682,0.05303588,0.02851609,0.08432348,-0.001467764,-0.08569061,-0.01156238,0.046454005,-0.020475674,0.05386696,-0.06596214,-0.01191215,0.07464592,-0.024295943,-0.045355592,0.091030516,0.024487648,0.007005313,0.116147384,-0.091230035,-0.032282222,-0.04530899,0.13070664,0.011833203,0.01889281,-0.020515868,-0.021417366,-0.011087468,0.05003917,-0.078220524,0.04361947,-0.044548646,0.014576094,0.039665513,0.02484668,-0.02909915,-0.0749781,-0.07724432,0.105442345,-0.06820107,-0.07966315,0.031998325,0.059366826,0.062728174,0.009606466,-0.006054736,4.0765104E-4,0.037477378,-0.019191511,-0.041450858,0.019275943,0.026209965,-0.0375179,-0.0012747799,-0.048626054,0.06904195,-0.059671763,0.025300099,-0.046614736,0.021113295,-0.009726836,0.02413886,0.027062483,0.01869183,-0.031440075,-0.006413887,-0.0034436157,-0.001645238,-0.009795695,0.030694554,-0.019311415,0.02112622,-0.020312387,0.0052388385,-0.05209975,-0.001