c({id:"CrunchForDeveloper:5",text:"Server-Side: Throwing Intercept for Subject Capabilities\nThe following is a typical example of throwing an intercept for a\ncapability required by the subject. (note that subject has a\ndistinction from user - CRUNCH is capable or providing capabilities\nfor a user when \"acting as\" another user)\n\nThe following snippet will not invoke an intercept because it is run\nas a script. If this code existed in a DAO decorator or a synchronous rule\nit would result in the client handling the intercept for you before\nre-sending (or aborting) the request.\n\njava\nimport foam.core.crunch.CapabilityIntercept;\nvar ex = new CapabilityIntercept();\nex.addCapabilityId(\"crunch.example\");\nthrow ex;",sourceId:"CrunchForDeveloper",kind:"flow",embeddingModel:"Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",vector:[0.039481334,0.018207358,-0.061243,0.031621013,0.019091152,-0.057320606,0.03229457,0.014013991,-0.09805887,-0.035361763,-0.007922503,-0.0633639,0.022592574,0.05880588,0.038365543,0.016350323,0.10304999,-0.02832141,-0.033470266,0.009499199,0.056095615,-0.025112092,0.051401746,-0.031493086,-0.051481213,-0.10352704,0.0025532073,-0.078197084,0.055211667,-0.004348634,0.08421879,0.004706902,0.021923153,-0.034643672,0.045708574,0.05467348,0.017455636,0.034133136,0.012869257,-0.02601654,-0.009924959,0.022634137,-0.028134251,-0.0069253356,0.0043174797,-0.063555755,-0.018066859,-0.028801331,-0.021023802,-0.010313339,0.012993205,3.2829863E-4,0.04576027,0.01574468,0.018116118,0.011545134,-0.04347259,0.046602562,-0.038624335,0.02281071,-0.06792937,-0.062049862,6.735102E-4,0.0071004326,0.08700602,0.058807995,0.06296985,-0.055313177,-0.09186912,0.029248744,-0.010716309,-0.069546424,-0.10408083,-0.05213814,0.06427811,0.052570663,-0.0033195443,0.028918756,0.060362086,0.017840328,-0.041358713,-0.032365672,-0.05834388,0.013023,-0.051383212,0.060422465,0.0033836975,-0.0019972902,0.08578707,0.048875492,-2.0380499E-4,-0.019376209,0.005356175,-0.016421793,-0.017769314,-0.04537621