c({id:"Dao:2",text:"Making a Class Storable\nTo store objects of a class in a DAO, FOAM needs to know which property (or properties) uniquely identify each object \u2014 the primary key.\n\nThe simplest approach is to name your key property id:\n\njavascript\nfoam.CLASS({\n  package: 'fun',\n  name: 'StoreMe',\n  properties: [ 'id', 'name' ],\n});\n\n\nIf your key property has a different name, or if you have a multi-part primary key, declare it explicitly with ids:\n\njavascript\nfoam.CLASS({\n  name: 'OrderLine',\n  ids: [ 'orderId', 'lineNumber' ],\n  properties: [ 'orderId', 'lineNumber', 'product', 'quantity' ],\n});\n\n\nIf you don't want to manage IDs yourself, use foam.dao.EasyDAO with seqNo: true and IDs will be assigned automatically.",sourceId:"Dao",kind:"flow",embeddingModel:"Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",vector:[-0.043958474,0.038969655,-0.07954144,0.001284581,-0.007619278,-0.004509531,0.08676119,-0.02884836,-0.0072642774,-0.09006693,-0.027911404,0.0074128513,-0.03917789,-0.05298926,0.059148986,0.039706368,-0.00600531,-0.017113877,-0.065321386,0.03240738,0.111225806,-0.0033200502,-0.031765472,7.9619273E-4,-0.069895975,0.062970534,0.060457453,-0.022803664,-0.040248845,-0.115175545,0.012509027,0.016993115,0.013459028,-0.017480014,0.014130922,-0.009950165,0.02747995,-0.028006371,0.03076134,0.012126294,0.0590381,-0.020247877,-0.01213456,-0.048175365,0.08191471,0.01305941,-0.06385947,0.024761014,0.077762574,0.01150749,-0.03357854,0.021768268,-0.025761861,0.06814785,-0.02412118,0.081062324,0.033965193,3.7592725E-4,-0.0410829,0.011513739,0.05190229,0.019067632,0.09855196,0.056807745,0.00796494,-0.020376462,0.015627416,0.035343006,-0.053341247,0.006748997,0.050876506,-0.0036768443,0.102164894,0.016829679,0.012655943,0.07138296,-0.010143325,0.011957409,0.07014044,0.046498347,-0.0899895,0.03558309,0.028230134,0.0206431,-0.0128346495,0.09971301,0.025704553,-0.021848522,-0.011613813,0.027907854,-0.07127667,-0.06160522,0.06800885,-0.025214938,0.015260801,0.046973206,0.05