c({id:"PropertyGotchas:7",text:"Two flags, two questions: transient means \"not stored\", searchable means \"may appear in a predicate\". A value resolved on read is legitimately both, so set searchable: true explicitly on a transient property that should stay queryable.\n\nTo expose a computed property to search while keeping it out of journals, use storageTransient: true alone. The literal transient flag stays false, so searchable stays true and networkTransient stays false.\n\nThe searchable gate is JS-only. SimpleQueryParser.js skips a non-searchable property, while the Java parser iterates getAxiomsByClass(PropertyInfo.class) and builds its name map with no searchable check at all (src/foam/parse/SimpleQueryParser.java:424-431) \u2014 a real client/server difference in accepted query syntax.\n\nA subclass override must reset the literal flag. An override clones the parent axiom, so a parent's literal transient: true rides along and keeps forcing networkTransient on the child. To narrow a fully-transient parent property to storage-only in one subclass, set BOTH transient: false and storageTransient: true \u2014 storageTransient: true alone changes nothing.\n\n---",sourceId:"PropertyGotchas",kind:"flow",embeddingModel:"Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",vector:[-0.07647198,0.011386533,-0.002099041,0.102577806,-0.0010513562,-0.020436173,-0.02536408,-0.0064614676,-0.006982019,-0.039218172,0.02331262,0.017722696,0.038256574,-0.015320101,-0.008475138,-0.1038395,0.0813099,-0.066596515,0.036311533,-0.021862201,0.014816455,-0.005059087,-0.025226105,-0.07319168,-0.037500605,0.05263421,-0.07311334,-0.16006275,0.05239025,-0.020095166,-0.024570717,0.043871988,-0.12824467,0.047235195,0.01854814,0.06055284,-0.0038097422,0.05636527,0.043632783,-0.053839806,-0.0010161872,-0.06684496,-0.05869282,-0.04373603,0.037047576,-0.018008206,0.03829673,-0.04676156,-0.09132596,-0.01587063,0.028892785,0.011915142,0.045632172,0.047819417,0.082616,0.03935936,-0.039214168,0.04027417,-0.076758005,-0.0485