c({id:"PushNotifications:3",text:"APNS (Apple) Push\nAPNS push is supported by he APNSPushService in core.\n\n1. To setup APNS push notification support, you need to first register your app with Apple <a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/usernotifications/registering-your-app-with-apns\"/>\n2. Then you need to obtain an SSL client certificate for authenticated to APNS from core. <a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/usernotifications/establishing-a-certificate-based-connection-to-apns\"/>\n3. \n\nYou then need to put your certificate and the associated private key into a .p12 file. If you followed instructions on the above link, you can export a .p12 from the Keychain Access app on macOS by finding the certificate, right clicking and selecting \"export\"\n\n4. Convert the .p12 file to base64 using the shell $ base64 -b 70 < push-credentials.p12 > push-credentials.p12.txt\n5. Save your apns credentials into a credentials.jrl file in your app/deployment \n\np({\n  \"class\": \"foam.core.notification.push.APNSCredential\",\n  \"id\": \"apns-sandbox-creds\",\n  \"host\": \"api.sandbox.push.apple.com\",\n  \"appBundleId\": \"my.app.bundle.id\",\n  \"p12Password\": \"password\",\n  \"p12Base64\": \"\"\"\n  RUtx+68Ctaqhaa5vFI7iUPG2IXo7hhPgSqFScdY02Rm9k4cQmeIaL3bfi2U3HwXi4msS+v\n  uIf4roiUOg3Us8m8RgHOkZr/GAbxDRqBS8DnD5PXbAp1VscBvvxI1cOG3bkd3ept5+TAQ/\n  jiVUqIsD0RhKdrpJ3UZ0naD...\n\"\"\"\n})\n\n\n6. Finally configure the APNSpushService to use the newly created credentials \n\np({\n  \"class\":\"foam.core.boot.CSpec\",\n  \"name\":\"APNSpushService\",\n  \"lazy\":true,\n  \"serve\":false,\n  \"service\":{\n    \"class\":\"foam.core.notification.push.APNSPushService\",\n    \"apnsCredentialId\": \"apns-sandbox-creds\"\n  }\n})",sourceId:"PushNotifications",kind:"flow",embeddingModel:"Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",vector:[-0.053447,-0.043825172,-0.048449643,-0.08011823,-0.083405346,-0.045623556,0.010197453,0.017383361,0.06148862,0.044912223,0.03244426,