c({id:"Refinements:1",text:"What are Refinements?\nRefinements allow you to extend or modify existing classes after they've been defined by adding new axioms to them. 1  When a model specifies a refines property, it doesn't create a new class but instead adds axioms to the existing class being refined. 1",sourceId:"Refinements",kind:"flow",embeddingModel:"Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",vector:[-0.06832463,-0.06287954,0.013486554,0.0055918763,0.022115342,0.0310246,0.004639701,-0.016531577,-0.02997188,0.024595167,-0.01662572,0.018549427,-0.012312578,-0.07096881,-0.004170524,-0.01889931,-0.0013567272,0.07809635,-0.09838163,-0.022061301,0.13600181,-0.032238103,-0.046684694,-0.001822518,-0.04953747,0.021383615,-0.050451223,-0.011431683,0.017497052,-0.0032039438,-0.0133547615,0.14070989,-0.06625915,0.039713982,-0.07025836,0.08836819,0.0857317,0.06617677,-0.02062894,0.064133175,-0.08366802,0.017716192,-0.0076071215,0.062651806,0.09067617,0.0037236328,0.06864765,-0.05213646,-0.01830618,-0.037741445,-0.050030153,-0.021033078,-0.12620471,0.036680993,0.059932627,0.09266011,0.033589642,0.03681187,-0.022598898,-0.085512556,-0.0019894578,-0.009485628,6.414857E-4,0.011938521,-0.03623926,0.0049926452,-0.1003261,0.022967324,0.04192838,-0.008083238,0.037632592,0.039236885,0.08772139,-0.032643665,0.032034744,-0.0021162697,-0.0013147688,0.10118426,0.051040724,0.011335006,-0.060597505,-0.05942254,0.03445955,-0.060364332,0.05795283,-0.03541233,0.005646757,-0.09742401,0.050613787,0.013431879,0.08533005,-0.010227787,-0.0060258433,-3.7582437E-4,-0.03342959,-0.004342162,-0.024877565,-0.06277429,0.015043183,0.020295065,-0.020679304,0.063439496,-0.0270061,0.017536566,-0.017617159,-0.081024446,-0.034100838,0.08152354,-0.084548846,-1.8192158E-4,0.021302138,-0.032948855,-0.0022698606,-0.08237673,0.030649947,0.012786991,-0.06097403,-0.11051761,0.009810975,-0.053117227,-0.011111335,0.13143705,0.08722391,0.021514582,0.08175217,-0.0024897058,-0.095836565,1.4596707E-33,-0.034898173,0.027601046,2.9057174E-4,