c({id:"Refinements:2",text:"How Refinements Work with Axioms\nWhen buildClass() encounters a model with a refines property, it looks up the existing class and adds the new axioms to it rather than creating a new class: 1\n\nThe key difference is that refinements call cls.installModel(this) on an existing class, which triggers the axiom installation process on that class. 2",sourceId:"Refinements",kind:"flow",embeddingModel:"Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",vector:[-0.082036845,-0.030457906,0.018099118,-0.030085614,0.038782082,-0.025330732,0.018855374,-0.014951122,-0.006355956,0.009850301,0.017215427,0.0024913626,0.013263243,-0.079439856,-0.0034336238,0.0044404287,0.023276087,0.0030846025,-0.045285214,-0.018153194,0.11850298,-0.047276422,-0.040419433,0.0034879765,-0.035011664,0.037847176,-0.007272478,0.009674152,0.06925632,-0.0031317754,-0.053569175,0.13226752,-0.04806616,0.0019426256,-0.061580267,0.1151387,0.10758928,0.041790962,-0.017901184,0.07230914,-0.08481776,0.045597963,0.02829402,0.013617444,0.07921514,-0.0023050464,0.031569414,-0.034705386,-0.028981123,-0.061068285,-0.025762796,0.003428012,-0.1142329,-0.014283766,0.084528886,0.16984119,0.044023585,0.039911978,-0.039383058,-0.1253708,-0.044394456,0.031184033,-0.024460418,0.055256926,-0.024741543,0.007067464,-0.05992012,-3.4226883E-5,0.073640145,2.0075715E-5,0.022844834,0.02471895,0.082688645,-0.021781264,0.012257115,0.029032527,0.063291505,0.10494906,0.038850825,0.00975984,-0.050682932,-6.955375E-4,0.02227799,-0.04833818,0.09505671,-0.03695744,0.061265074,-0.10418084,0.048429172,0.04555162,0.116416916,-0.020361738,-0.038069755,0.023805441,-0.02620867,0.04574237,-0.0037844984,2.1992998E-4,-0.011046416,0.024942406,-0.019788003,0.055427626,0.019034695,-0.013260198,-0.0017045843,-0.042656373,-0.05447133,0.038277093,-0.047538728,-0.0044605676,0.029307213,-0.08127822,-0.0059838193,-0.07235944,-0.013486983,0.035927996,-0.04481101,-0.10919335,0.015128767,0.0057668467,-0.0028305291,0.09633448,0.044931345,-0.045719173,0.056092