c({id:"Relationships:0",text:"Relationships\nCovers FOAM Relationships (1:many, many:many): foam.RELATIONSHIP syntax, generated FK properties, filtered DAOs, junction models.\n\nKeywords: relationship, foreign key, junction, dao, cardinality, knowledge\n\n<flow name=\"Relationships\" category=\"DOC/GUIDE\" spid=\"foam\" description=\"Covers FOAM Relationships (1:many, many:many): foam.RELATIONSHIP syntax, generated FK properties, filtered DAOs, junction models.\" keywords=\"relationship,foreign key,junction,dao,cardinality,knowledge\"/>\n\n<!-- START doctoc generated TOC please keep comment here to allow auto update -->\n<!-- DON'T EDIT THIS SECTION, INSTEAD RE-RUN doctoc TO UPDATE -->\nTable of Contents  generated with DocToc\n\n- FOAM Relationships\n  - Overview\n  - Reference vs Relationship\n    - Reference Property\n    - Relationship\n    - Comparison Table\n    - Real-World Example\n  - Defining a Relationship\n    - Basic Syntax\n    - Relationship Properties\n  - One-to-Many Relationships (1:)\n    - What Gets Generated\n    - Example: Professor \u2192 Courses\n    - Using the Relationship\n  - Many-to-Many Relationships (:*)\n    - What Gets Generated\n    - Example: Student \u2194 Course\n    - The Generated Junction Model\n    - Using the ManyToManyRelationship\n  - How FOAM Eliminates Junction API Complexity\n    - Traditional Junction Table Approach\n    - FOAM's Approach\n  - Advanced Configuration\n    - Custom Property Configuration\n    - Custom DAO Keys\n    - One-Way Relationships\n  - UI Integration\n  - Complete Working Example\n    - Models\n    - Services Configuration\n    - Usage in Application Code\n  - Summary\n\n<!-- END doctoc generated TOC please keep comment here to allow auto update -->",sourceId:"Relationships",kind:"flow",embeddingModel:"Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",vector:[0.0037539836,-0.034343444,-0.049122166,0.02499922,0.015090314,0.014370624,-0.042591188,-0.041968714,-0.017537354,-0.01662406,0.014734033,-0.06994359,0.09736288,0.00