c({id:"SPID:8",text:"User-SPID Lifecycle\n1. User Creation\n\njavascript\n// User created without SPID\nvar user = User.create({\n  email: 'john@example.com',\n  firstName: 'John'\n});\nawait userDAO.put(user);\n// User initially sees data from their theme's SPID\n\n\n2. SPID Assignment\n\njavascript\n// Admin assigns SPID to user\nuser.spid = 'acme';\nawait userDAO.put(user);\n// Triggers CreateUserCapabilityJunctionOnSpidSet rule\n// Which calls ServiceProvider.setupSpid(x, user)\n\n\n3. What setupSpid() Does\n\n1. Gets the capability path for the ServiceProvider\n2. Creates/updates UserCapabilityJunction records\n3. Sets junction status to GRANTED\n4. User now has serviceprovider.read.acme permission\n\n4. SPID Change\n\njavascript\n// Admin changes user's SPID\nuser.spid = 'newcorp';\nawait userDAO.put(user);\n// 1. removeSpid() called for old SPID ('acme')\n// 2. setupSpid() called for new SPID ('newcorp')\n// User can now only see 'newcorp' data",sourceId:"SPID",kind:"flow",embeddingModel:"Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",vector:[-0.1167028,-0.06065539,-0.03971976,-0.00970506,-0.042853978,-0.007630536,0.1176335,0.02846186,-0.017733697,-0.032657906,0.05585656,0.046198174,0.06670668,-0.020183831,-0.013452463,0.072885565,0.029813865,-0.09427651,-0.039861564,-0.046511963,0.07590308,-0.12057128,-0.052191373,-0.056354567,-0.012772044,-0.051722966,0.0126134725,-0.027237171,0.0466544,0.0898582,0.13367778,-0.02259454,-0.0034177443,-0.08176996,0.010521938,0.0076178955,0.09131419,0.018637879,0.01622992,0.03347196,-0.026363723,0.034669492,-0.039671686,-0.005479195,0.071300685,-0.013471588,-0.006968345,0.019019168,-0.053006217,0.031118901,0.021675838,-0.031659734,0.02270613,-0.009193538,-0.030967612,0.05512253,-0.021018917,0.08253616,-0.017547065,-0.015344855,-0.05385384,-0.058820933,0.02858139,0.030019557,0.042529095,-0.06918933,0.025470639,-0.11399738,0.041404445,-0.07233266,-0.043014277,0.09514596,-0.04757845,0.027157433,0.0056249807,-0.043568682,4.9369363E-4,0.12976877,-0.0024