c({id:"Services:2",text:"But from the client's point of view, the stub/network/skeleton is transparent and it looks like they're just magically calling the server service directly:\n\nClient Code -> Service Server\n\nSo, normally there is no work that needs to be done to implement the client-side service, as the stub does this by delegating across the network to the server implementation. However, you can decorate the default client service if you want to add some client-side functionality like caching.\n\n5. In your code, import the service\nEg:\n\nimports: [\n  'stack', 'userDAO', 'user', 'auth'\n],\n\nNow, you can call the service in your code:\n\nthis.auth.login(\"marc4@marc.com\", \"marc123\").then(function(response) {\n  console.log(response);\n}",sourceId:"Services",kind:"flow",embeddingModel:"Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",vector:[-0.13757822,0.042368293,-0.0056258845,-0.024963196,-0.09149141,-0.06845162,-0.0023070935,0.027312117,0.041959584,-0.018994724,-0.04906238,0.10087964,-0.039772462,0.019018594,0.10352223,-0.038580664,0.084489085,9.467899E-4,0.04640249,-0.050360903,0.06312722,-0.039591543,-0.07499645,0.015705582,-0.0033030454,-0.1159854,0.043822248,-0.098349705,-0.0045819385,0.0011056092,0.11160723,-0.016081378,-0.078167774,-0.025607757,-0.14375134,0.044356342,-0.032778367,-0.028747924,0.029683415,0.01960827,0.046417814,0.01906992,-0.08988037,0.009665696,0.019217914,-0.050599836,0.009967877,0.01573384,-0.048590824,0.020900872,-0.028312745,-0.05691826,0.022226337,0.05577552,-0.07041603,-0.020768026,-0.045429643,0.016904993,-0.011485533,0.049924407,0.040926833,-0.09028422,0.10838909,0.036187533,0.05887026,-0.016800117,-0.01726909,0.027056642,-0.049677517,-0.017808016,0.009458055,0.009579644,0.01602683,-0.0134260785,-0.0073646684,-0.015952773,-0.084708385,-0.0053515136,0.03366803,5.7562056E-4,0.04074505,-0.054362398,-0.035185948,0.07588754,0.0055022645,0.071862385,0.020036256,-0.02685323,-0.014236744,-0.032350276,0.04479577,0.045658004,-0.0058489935,-0.0463509