c({id:"U3:4",text:"Building DOM \u2014 start(), end(), add(), tag()\nAll DOM building happens inside a render() method via method chaining:\n\njavascript\nfoam.CLASS({\n  name: 'MyView',\n  extends: 'foam.u2.View',\n  methods: [\n    function render() {\n      this.SUPER();\n      this\n        .addClass()                                  // adds scoped root CSS class\n        .start('section')                            // <section>\n          .start('h2').add(this.data.title$).end()  //   <h2>reactive title</h2>\n          .start('ul')                               //   <ul>\n            .start('li').add('Item 1').end()         //     <li>Item 1</li>\n            .start('li').add('Item 2').end()         //     <li>Item 2</li>\n          .end()                                     //   </ul>\n        .end();                                      // </section>\n    }\n  ]\n});\n\n\nstart(spec, args, slot) / end()\n\nstart() pushes a new child element onto the build stack and returns it. end() returns to the parent. spec can be:\n\n- A tag name string: start('span')\n- A class or ViewSpec: start(this.MyView), start({class: 'foam.u2.TextField'})\n- A slot returning a ViewSpec: start(this.viewSpec$) \u2014 dynamic component\n\ntag(spec, args)\n\nShorthand for start(spec, args).end(). Use for self-contained components and void elements:\n\njavascript\nthis.tag('br');\nthis.tag('img', { src: this.imgUrl$, alt: this.name$ });\nthis.tag(this.MyWidget, { data: this.record });\n\n\nbr() / nbsp()\n\njavascript\nthis.add('Line 1').br().add('Line 2');\nthis.add('foo').nbsp().add('bar');   // non-breaking space\n\n\n---",sourceId:"U3",kind:"flow",embeddingModel:"Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",vector:[-0.06323222,0.0010146279,0.04772831,0.058922797,0.028286446,0.014211818,0.021508805,0.013282686,0.06589554,-0.05742672,0.020861123,-0.020824086,-0.02982302,-0.03724757,0.087400205,0.045752574,-0.053945135,-0.05848739,-0.06866291,0.007360244,0.08225939,-0.019651547,0.03583632,-0.037621517,-0