c({id:"U3:5",text:"add() Polymorphism\nadd() is the central method. It accepts anything and dispatches appropriately:\n\n| What you pass | What happens |\n|---------------|-------------|\n| null / undefined | Silently ignored |\n| Array | Each element added recursively |\n| String, Number | Creates a Text node \u2014 never raw HTML injection |\n| A Slot (obj.prop$) | Creates a SlotNode \u2014 updates DOM when slot changes |\n| A plain function(a, b, c) | Converted to ExpressionSlot watching a, b, c from this, wrapped in FunctionNode |\n| A DynamicFunction | Creates a FunctionNode |\n| A Promise | Wrapped in PromiseSlot; content replaces when promise resolves |\n| An Element | Appended directly |\n| An FObject with toE() | Calls toE() \u2014 all FObjects have this via FObjectToERefinement |\n| An FObject without toE() | Creates an isolated DetailView |\n| Object with addToE | Calls addToE(this) |\n\njavascript\n// Static text\nthis.add('Hello, world');\n\n// Reactive: updates when slot changes\nthis.add(this.data.name$);\n\n// Reactive function: re-runs when firstName or lastName changes\nthis.add(function(firstName, lastName) {\n  this.start('b').add(firstName + ' ' + lastName).end();\n});\n\n// Promise\nthis.add(this.loadData());   // DOM updates when promise resolves\n\n// Slot of elements\nthis.add(this.selectedView$);\n\n\n---",sourceId:"U3",kind:"flow",embeddingModel:"Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",vector:[-0.110051,0.0071718,0.0176707,0.07246796,-0.037938304,0.019082196,0.004800129,0.025215348,0.090602145,-0.021452013,-0.0013598956,-0.0473018,-0.0676365,-0.060509518,0.04597852,0.1026146,-0.012008576,-0.026525823,-0.06726484,-0.059601873,0.09298057,-0.077753656,-0.010954594,-0.01843187,-0.0033893683,0.055488843,-0.02011263,-0.024668548,0.037025873,-0.07274612,0.014039062,0.026497075,-0.010105325,0.056217242,-0.1459593,0.055173796,-0.053938404,0.0023636834,0.052044146,-0.035682045,0.06422872,0.035336364,-0.036417123,-0.0055358447,0.044051178,-0.016383626,-0.030204322,