c({id:"U3:13",text:"Property Rendering \u2014 Four Forms\nThere are four ways to put a property in the DOM, each with different behavior:\n\n| Form | What it renders | Honors permissions? |\n|------|----------------|---------------------|\n| OBJ.PROPNAME | Bare view (the property's configured view:) | No |\n| OBJ.PROPNAME. | PropertyBorder: view + label + validation + units | Yes |\n| obj.propName$ | Reactive value via SlotNode | N/A |\n| obj.propName | Static current value (snapshot) | N/A |\n\njavascript\n// In a render() with context data = invoice:\nthis.add(Invoice.AMOUNT)       // bare amount input/display; no label\nthis.add(Invoice.AMOUNT.)    // full field: label + input + validation + units\nthis.add(invoice.amount$)      // reactive number \u2014 updates but no label/input\nthis.add(invoice.amount)       // snapshot number \u2014 won't update\n\n\nPROPNAME (uppercase) gives the property axiom. . is a getter that wraps it in PropertyBorder, where permission checks and visibility rules run.\n\nImportant: writePermissionRequired: true is enforced only inside PropertyBorder. If you use the bare PROPNAME form, all users get RW regardless of what the model declares.\n\nFor compact display without a label but still permission-gated:\njavascript\n.tag(Invoice.AMOUNT., { config: { label: '', reserveLabelSpace: false } })\n\n\n---",sourceId:"U3",kind:"flow",embeddingModel:"Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",vector:[-0.1004615,0.08066209,-0.055421114,0.057314176,-0.021540996,0.023750702,-0.0026657037,0.0038625945,0.03651368,-0.022646723,0.023077453,-0.07229153,0.034228124,-0.011823004,0.04283812,0.06677281,0.07588207,-0.06013587,-0.08015552,0.01259716,0.06351884,-0.06647707,0.03089594,-0.024467723,0.019048521,0.05018697,-0.02661635,-0.022749003,0.08279936,-0.03269756,0.02461154,0.038566347,-0.02796523,-0.018669754,-0.007815965,0.004283846,0.049185842,0.08897044,0.0020287044,-0.009226076,0.022094235,-0.007608796,-0.021200038,-0.057784468,-0.014632905,-0.0062194336,0.021338135,