c({id:"Updating Objects in DAOs:3",text:"Quick Start\nTo change a stored object, read it, copy it, edit the copy, then write the copy back:\n\njavascript\nvar obj   = await dao.find(id);   // 1. read  (the returned object is frozen)\nvar clone = obj.clone();          // 2. copy  (a mutable duplicate)\nclone.status = 'DONE';            // 3. edit  (set the exact property)\nawait dao.put(clone);             // 4. write (this is the save)\n\n\nThe put is the step people miss. A DAO does not watch your object for changes. It only records what you hand back to it. No put, no update.\n\n---",sourceId:"Updating Objects in DAOs",kind:"flow",embeddingModel:"Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",vector:[-0.07117529,-0.020939447,-0.021013185,0.0945672,-0.034685776,-0.03186651,-0.030433727,-0.024769481,0.028264184,0.025893213,-0.047861952,0.055840537,-0.11356286,-0.087384894,-0.05292914,0.042018548,0.054980062,0.047617406,-0.08531716,0.033853278,0.041920133,-0.08666564,0.011452884,-0.014755517,0.066781975,0.03084746,0.054119725,-0.021866133,-0.0018422488,-0.066591896,-0.045637943,-0.044654623,-0.045034036,-0.022069508,-0.01017396,0.08618597,-0.0018752416,-0.01588453,0.056711737,-0.070638664,0.07312382,0.0016669922,-0.04314982,0.0014320448,0.02471118,0.03943312,-0.030187603,0.03190968,0.043303248,-0.047183584,-0.030771313,-0.041587844,-0.07353658,0.027560191,-0.0013262521,0.07945235,0.11462112,0.031630613,-0.062235117,0.006695603,0.024187207,0.048799407,0.08895601,0.07039205,0.05999228,0.024210773,0.038802303,-0.03329773,0.012307098,-0.032431964,0.035786968,0.078350276,0.067818515,-9.224018E-4,-0.0013810211,-0.060037393,0.011173613,0.06043809,0.026238732,0.019381989,2.903588E-4,-0.038376473,0.019291248,0.036381733,-0.03873152,0.011176764,0.07288763,0.011173639,0.04242668,0.009562058,-0.07453306,0.005894634,0.05469411,-0.04653915,-0.084747076,0.011750392,0.05981499,0.0943702,0.02155077,0.013976707,0.058120146,0.09903061,-0.01200073,0.010756259,-0.0027451338,-0.09588861,0.06655282,-0.07536191,