c({id:"Updating Objects in DAOs:4",text:"Overview\nWhat It Does\n\nA DAO (Data Access Object) is the read/write interface to a collection of objects. Updating works the same way as creating: you call put with an object that carries the id you want to replace. The DAO overwrites the stored value with the one you pass.\n\nThe twist is that objects coming out of a DAO are frozen. You cannot edit them in place. You clone first, edit the clone, and put the clone back.\n\nKey Files\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| foam/lang/FObject.js | Defines clone and copyFrom for the JavaScript side |\n| foam/lang/FObject.java | Defines fclone; throws Object is frozen. from assertNotFrozen |\n| foam/dao/MDAO.java | In-memory DAO; clones and freezes objects on store |\n| foam/dao/MapDAO.java | Map-backed DAO; calls obj.freeze() on store |\n| foam/dao/FreezingDAO.js | Decorator that freezes objects passing through |\n\n---",sourceId:"Updating Objects in DAOs",kind:"flow",embeddingModel:"Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",vector:[-0.07485423,0.041073,-0.048522923,0.044131186,-0.033236288,-0.09831844,0.015998472,0.023754248,-0.044535536,0.0059651122,-0.023779666,0.022453105,-0.054654226,-0.09085135,0.006904283,0.037682157,0.003248693,0.024263982,-0.07949603,0.07062253,0.085262395,-0.029829584,-0.06328008,-0.035133533,0.016497774,0.0471036,0.043179076,-0.06658478,-0.031630322,-0.07912069,-0.013465215,0.022749074,-0.04697228,-0.023944173,0.005200518,0.11526902,0.037864532,-0.04972855,0.026601499,-0.062683925,0.029208863,0.041888904,-0.06989599,-0.012421203,0.012878127,0.06697529,-0.008749442,0.01893254,0.03458228,-0.025419299,-0.039913602,-0.015493538,-0.047901332,0.058384225,-0.035715826,0.04518894,0.078217305,0.0069928193,-0.05586267,0.0034010648,5.4460205E-4,0.06332489,0.11275253,0.1103035,0.054296695,-0.044777166,0.021423612,-0.008827697,0.016375527,-0.0332866,-0.0053157676,0.049532983,0.07713752,-0.011420251,0.03811282,-0.011933854,-0.05241354,0.07411191,0.10737554,-0.01957191,0.0385