c({id:"Updating Objects in DAOs:9",text:"javascript\nvar sink = await dao.where(M.EQ(MyModel.PROCESSED, false)).select();\nfor ( var row of sink.array ) {\n  var clone = row.clone();   // each row from select() is frozen\n  clone.processed = true;\n  await dao.put(clone);\n}\n\nThe same rule as the single-object case applies per row: clone, edit the clone, put the clone. Putting row directly would either fail on the frozen instance or write back an object the DAO still shares.\n\nChoosing find versus select\n\n| Need | Use |\n|------|-----|\n| One object by id | dao.find(id) |\n| One object by predicate | dao.find(predicate) |\n| A list to iterate | dao.select(new ArraySink()) |",sourceId:"Updating Objects in DAOs",kind:"flow",embeddingModel:"Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",vector:[-0.09539029,-0.04763082,0.009682573,0.07975685,-0.038012825,-0.08145046,-0.013214549,-0.056810576,0.01510775,0.014436736,-0.02743077,0.035022408,-0.048543725,-0.0725262,-0.0563936,0.071249045,0.035918873,0.021016994,-0.02481174,0.004541268,0.09887187,-0.040765613,-0.042254943,-0.055475067,0.038976606,0.07118569,0.07353607,-0.081977464,0.02103714,-0.052893937,-0.11174634,0.00122575,-0.08969755,-0.012916639,-0.011473437,0.04509861,-0.040844094,-0.017898245,0.048780285,-0.032383423,0.108528286,0.03201339,0.009954713,-0.059625637,0.046106283,0.012640248,-0.06482787,0.04248327,0.02460131,-0.052016076,-0.05514847,-0.001493884,-0.016726082,0.031641264,0.04569946,0.008137714,0.074882306,-0.040426105,-0.068767555,0.00887545,0.03845438,0.024866356,0.032215785,0.06811565,0.129864,-0.010031798,0.06007881,0.04513509,0.017770724,0.031075263,0.002007142,0.066109315,0.051308595,0.030531665,0.008427174,-0.017300142,0.100027755,-0.007786125,0.017415479,0.07066109,-0.048782688,0.014263124,-0.025166493,-0.017036233,-0.08898337,0.01202083,0.01832469,-0.030429682,0.07257928,-0.010596353,-0.09837192,0.028961733,0.09079377,-0.04043062,-0.026336227,0.011920402,0.056728676,0.072026715,0.018191563,-0.0055623045,0.00820440