c({id:"VsSpring:18",text:"axioms: [\n      {\n        name: 'axiom1',\n        installInClass: function(cls) { ... },\n        installInProto: function(proto) { ... }\n      }\n    ]\n  });\n</pre>\n  Axioms can be added either during the initial creation of a class and prototype,\n  or anytime after.  This allows classes to be extended with new functionality,\n  and this is very important to the bootstrap process because it allows us to\n  start out with very simple definitions of Model and FObject, and then build\n  them up until they're fully bootstrapped.\n<p>\n  However, raw axioms are rarely used directly. Instead we model higher-level\n  axiom types, including:\n<ul>\n  <li>Requires   - Require other classes\n  <li>Imports    - Context imports\n  <li>Exports    - Context exports\n  <li>Implements - Declare interfaces implemented / mix-ins mixed-in\n  <li>Constants  - Add constants to the prototype and class\n  <li>Properties - High-level instance variable definitions\n  <li>Methods    - Prototype methods\n  <li>Topics     - Publish/sub topics\n  <li>Listeners  - Like methods, but with extra features for use as callbacks\n</ul>\n\nFile: doc/guides/REQUIRESVSIMPORTS.md (L19-51)\nmarkdown",sourceId:"VsSpring",kind:"flow",embeddingModel:"Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",vector:[-0.088129416,-0.020710632,0.005697693,-0.009941481,0.084001705,-0.010824598,-0.06564184,0.069591135,-0.047331505,-0.010555973,-0.008770438,-0.005113438,0.009524554,-0.0034616755,0.08038319,-0.01423288,0.060127206,-0.0105164135,-0.048554294,0.04636195,0.077376865,-0.043267448,-0.008750239,-0.0107612815,-0.10497689,0.008217155,0.037961263,-0.035021316,0.032284368,-0.018755766,-0.025227036,0.058200974,-0.02052955,0.025933191,-0.057430442,0.0643657,0.034060102,-0.045584068,-0.054484647,0.009258856,-0.021941308,-0.07729965,-0.005056716,0.004140743,0.062102262,-0.048960894,0.029953841,-0.10120266,-0.011636012,-0.03495031,-0.011464959,0.019857457,-0.0025083038,0.037455183,0.07880593,0.01596611,0.02900710