c({id:"VsWebComponents:7",text:"FOAM's approach demonstrated that you could achieve the same goals \u2014 encapsulated, reusable components with reactive properties \u2014 using existing browser standards (the DOM, JavaScript classes, CSS) and a small library on top. The library approach is more agile, more fixable, and iteration happens at development speed rather than standards-committee speed.\n\nThis turned out to be exactly the trajectory that the Polymer team itself eventually took: Lit is essentially an acknowledgement that a small library over the existing platform is the right answer, and that the complex parts of Web Components (especially HTML Imports, which was abandoned entirely) did not need to be standards at all.",sourceId:"VsWebComponents",kind:"flow",embeddingModel:"Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",vector:[-0.077969,-0.03043325,0.022017805,0.04034214,0.06821108,-0.0011215283,-0.07062975,0.009009588,-0.056378603,-0.03331507,-0.054532304,0.04912786,-0.02532359,0.07404303,0.09128882,0.025527945,0.062470168,-0.034849625,0.019968623,0.042667124,0.0036876197,-0.07054726,0.012869389,-0.010422133,-0.037037734,0.07952986,-0.035626482,-0.09453604,0.053313266,-0.08365722,0.03940355,0.040951088,0.012428215,-0.035254426,-0.06397105,0.04812824,0.014094605,-0.023124628,-0.087115444,0.011929382,0.0043032845,-0.047015883,-0.023102662,-0.0239026,-0.006049547,-0.079966895,-0.036923137,-0.05445711,-0.075590804,-0.024812158,-0.0061463234,-0.10937222,0.02294125,-0.06260684,-0.01182532,0.030081026,0.036357287,-0.02356808,0.03494701,-0.042508513,-0.049806748,0.018215794,0.04150042,0.072259806,0.026384754,0.04175117,0.015104259,0.045406684,0.03240722,0.002992049,-0.06576194,0.0048735817,0.08994621,0.011081036,0.037888076,-0.017179053,-9.219942E-5,-0.011230356,0.014022931,0.023401195,-0.005010668,0.049260378,0.0216384,0.060936633,0.073440485,0.09485415,0.11126617,-0.032887127,-0.034160543,-0.023473829,0.024330324,-0.005414944,0.08131922,0.031334743,-0.04510632,0.003479009,0.0308859