c({id:"manual:AScript:5",text:"Making decisions\nThis is the part you'll use most. The test in an IF or IFS is a condition \u2014 see Writing conditions above, and the Query Syntax Guide for everything you can put there.\n\nIF \u2014 one test\n\nIF(test, value-if-true, value-if-false)\n\n\nIF(amount > 10000, \"review\", \"auto\")\nIF(balance < 0, \"OVERDRAWN\", \"OK\")\n\n\nIFS \u2014 several tests in order\n\nIFS(test1, value1, test2, value2, \u2026) \u2014 returns the value for the first test that is true. End with true as a catch-all \"otherwise\":\n\n\nIFS(\n  balance > 1000, \"high\",\n  balance > 500,  \"medium\",\n  true,           \"low\"\n)\n\n\nSWITCH \u2014 match one value against options\n\nSWITCH(value, option1, result1, option2, result2, \u2026, otherwise)\n\n\nSWITCH(currency, \"USD\", \"$\", \"EUR\", \"\u20ac\", \"GBP\", \"\u00a3\", \"?\")\n\n\n---",sourceId:"manual:AScript",kind:"flow",embeddingModel:"Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",vector:[-0.008116259,0.091763966,-0.051071864,0.012117305,-0.03518481,-0.04300824,0.09347339,0.049890604,0.00810943,0.02226966,0.012845473,-0.16468328,-0.0052569173,0.010252561,0.0527797,-0.0243821,0.0035294266,0.00238914,-0.052309323,0.0034961049,0.07835247,-0.060337067,-0.08180408,0.0027710253,0.011577083,0.0457757,0.04437585,0.020637874,-0.022432942,-0.0033319371,-0.081645414,0.03669008,0.0076546767,0.0107200015,-0.0027164074,-0.042105667,-0.01461128,-0.002592373,-0.05105466,-0.030209996,-0.08871191,-0.092889555,0.051089503,-0.08431264,0.04011506,0.09006152,-0.031060418,0.13791473,-0.044867203,0.04288568,0.03860111,0.016671747,5.0326544E-5,0.0029553673,0.009103632,0.04488238,0.025280442,-0.051846832,0.001170026,-0.027843973,-0.05301295,-0.023097912,-0.016957462,-0.015493726,0.032373354,0.026219634,-0.0465797,-0.03460379,-0.055419225,0.07702408,-0.02243754,-0.05123372,-0.026967905,0.011634515,-0.022356104,0.048622694,0.07034393,-0.060851052,-0.03286671,0.035107512,-0.03720576,-0.04769855,-0.054244295,0.009303443,0.084637366,-